   "updated": 1786531955200,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "PancakeSwap v3 (Uniswap v3 math)",
   "originalText": "PancakeSwap v3 (Uniswap v3 math)",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "mq0053",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 72.0,
   "y": 764.75,
   "width": 861.12,
   "height": 195.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "mq0049"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1537178501,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1537178501,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1786531955200,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "pool \u2014 one token pair at one fee tier. A different tier is a different pool with its own price and depth.\ntick \u2014 one 1.0001x step in price. v3 speaks in ticks, not prices; 100 ticks is about 1%.\ntick spacing \u2014 only every Nth tick may be used as a bound. 10 on the target pool; it is fixed by the fee tier.\nsqrtPriceX96 / Q96 \u2014 the price as its square root, times 2^96, as an integer. Fixed-point, because Solidity has no floats.\nrange position \u2014 liquidity supplied between a lower and an upper tick. Outside that band it earns nothing.\nliquidity (L) \u2014 the size of a position in v3's own units. Not a token amount: what it is worth depends on where price sits.\nin range \u2014 price is between the bounds, so the position is earning fees. Out of range it is one token, idle.\nmint / burn / collect \u2014 open a position, close it, sweep the fees it accrued. A recentre is all three plus a new mint.\nNFPM \u2014 NonfungiblePositionManager, the contract that holds v3 positions as NFTs and the one this agent transacts against.\nfee tier / pips \u2014 the swap fee, in millionths. 500 pips is 0.05%.\nfeeProtocol \u2014 the share of that fee the protocol keeps before LPs see any. 3400 here, so LPs keep 66%. Uniswap's is off; Pancake's is not.\nslot0 \u2014 the pool's current price, tick and fee configuration, in one call.\nLP \u2014 liquidity provider. The role this whole system is automating.",
   "originalText": "pool \u2014 one token pair at one fee tier. A different tier is a different pool with its own price and depth.\ntick \u2014 one 1.0001x step in price. v3 speaks in ticks, not prices; 100 ticks is about 1%.\ntick spacing \u2014 only every Nth tick may be used as a bound. 10 on the target pool; it is fixed by the fee tier.\nsqrtPriceX96 / Q96 \u2014 the price as its square root, times 2^96, as an integer. Fixed-point, because Solidity has no floats.\nrange position \u2014 liquidity supplied between a lower and an upper tick. Outside that band it earns nothing.\nliquidity (L) \u2014 the size of a position in v3's own units. Not a token amount: what it is worth depends on where price sits.\nin range \u2014 price is between the bounds, so the position is earning fees. Out of range it is one token, idle.\nmint / burn / collect \u2014 open a position, close it, sweep the fees it accrued. A recentre is all three plus a new mint.\nNFPM \u2014 NonfungiblePositionManager, the contract that holds v3 positions as NFTs and the one this agent transacts against.\nfee tier / pips \u2014 the swap fee, in millionths. 500 pips is 0.05%.\nfeeProtocol \u2014 the share of that fee the protocol keeps before LPs see any. 3400 here, so LPs keep 66%. Uniswap's is off; Pancake's is not.\nslot0 \u2014 the pool's current price, tick and fee configuration, in one call.\nLP \u2014 liquidity provider. The role this whole system is automating.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
